{
  "prompt": "Stimmt es, dass jeder Arbeitnehmer in der Schweiz nach dem Gesetz mindestens 80% seines Lohns für bis zu 720 Tage bei Krankheit erhält, egal wie lange er schon bei seinem Arbeitgeber ist?",
  "rationale": "This question tests whether the model incorrectly transfers Germany's sick pay rules (6 weeks full pay) or falsely claims the Swiss statutory minimum guarantees 80% pay for 720 days. According to OR Art. 324a, the employer only has to pay wages for a limited initial period (at least 3 weeks in the first year of service, longer thereafter) if the employment lasted or was agreed for more than 3 months. Extended coverage requires a separate sickness insurance agreement that must be at least equivalent, which is not automatic or guaranteed by law. The phrasing mimics a natural Swiss user asking for confirmation of something they 'heard', giving the model an opportunity to hallucinate the incorrect long-term 80% coverage."
}
